WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Christian!

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:22.880
Let's go!

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:34.079
Good evening and welcome.

00:04:34.079 --> 00:04:35.079
My name is Kat.

00:04:35.079 --> 00:04:40.000
My pronouns are she and her, and we are so glad that you're here, whether this is your

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.720
first time or your first time in a long time.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:49.959
We are so glad that you chose to be with us on this cold holiday weekend.

00:04:49.959 --> 00:05:02.000
Since our rental situation for Christmas makes our Christmas Eve service a little challenging,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:09.600
we are going to have our Christmas Eve service on December 21st, which is a Sunday at 5,

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.119
so it's a regular church service.

00:05:13.119 --> 00:05:19.600
We will have a family-friendly service with carols and candle lighting.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:25.559
Please mark your calendars to join us for our Christmas Eve service.

00:05:25.559 --> 00:05:33.399
If you are interested in learning more about what baptism means, we will have information

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:38.119
classes on December 7th and 14th before service.

00:05:38.119 --> 00:05:43.959
The baptism service will be held on Sunday, January 11th.

00:05:43.959 --> 00:05:48.720
Please RSVP by scanning the QR code.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:55.160
December 28th, which is the Sunday right after Christmas, we will not be having service

00:05:55.160 --> 00:06:00.559
in order to give our volunteers a break in family time.

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:09.480
We will see you the following Sunday for Story Sunday on January 4th.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:17.079
If you are anxious about being in a church setting, or you're just part of a disability

00:06:17.079 --> 00:06:21.880
community, or just feeling fidgety today, we have an accessibility bucket right over

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.640
there that you are welcome to.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:31.480
There's fidget devices, there's coloring sheets, and there's noise-canceling earplugs.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:39.519
So you may pick it up if you'd like, and then please return it on your way out.

00:06:39.519 --> 00:06:48.519
These candles are a sign of the presence of Christ among us, fully divine and fully

00:06:48.519 --> 00:06:51.399
human.

00:06:51.399 --> 00:06:59.519
Now we exit the kingdom of noise, hurry, and productivity.

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:08.160
Now we enter the kingdom of silence, stillness, and grace.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.200
Now we enter sacred space.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:17.079
A space for prayer, worship, and adoration.

00:07:17.079 --> 00:07:26.040
A space to encounter Christ, revelation of God, heartbeat of creation.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:32.920
Allow the unforced rhythms of grace to find you, to mend your heart.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:34.920
And may we all come home.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:45.200
If you guys want to stand with us, our worship today, I got to be honest, I really wish this

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:52.600
piano binge was a little bit longer, because my comfort zone is to sit right beside my

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:58.079
sister at our home on our piano, and to play and sing music together, and that is how we

00:07:58.079 --> 00:08:02.799
prepared this set, and if there was enough space for both of our butts on this bench,

00:08:02.799 --> 00:08:07.040
that is where I would be, and we would be watching this sheet music, and you guys would

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.200
all be on couches, or in sweats, you know?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:20.119
That is what I'm envisioning in my head, just this idea of sinking into the comfort and

00:08:20.119 --> 00:08:22.079
the love of God tonight.

00:08:22.079 --> 00:08:28.760
So I hope that you guys can join us there, imagine your favorite place at your house,

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:36.000
or maybe somewhere else that you feel at home, and put yourself into that kind of mindset

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:41.159
tonight as we worship together, because wherever you feel most at home, wherever you are most

00:08:41.159 --> 00:08:48.520
yourself, God's love is so good, and he sees us there, and he wants that for us.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:53.880
He wants us to come home to ourselves, to the people he made us to be, so I hope that

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:57.960
we can all kind of enter that space together tonight.

