00:14:56.119 --> 00:15:00.119
Jesus, for this city of Sachse, Texas, and for every city and community

00:15:00.119 --> 00:15:04.119
and all who live in them, we pray to you.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:08.280
For the good earth you have given us and the wisdom and the will

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:12.280
to conserve it, we pray to you.

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:16.280
For the old and the sick, for the widow and the orphan,

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:20.280
for the injured and suffering, we pray to you.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:24.280
For the poor and the oppressed, the unemployed

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:28.280
and destitute, for prisoners and captives

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:32.280
and all who remember and care for them, we pray to you.

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:36.440
For the vulnerable, the marginalized, and those unjustly

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:40.440
targeted for their gender, sexuality, race,

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:44.440
or other perceived difference, we pray to you.

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:48.440
For those experiencing loss, loneliness, and disconnection

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:52.440
and for those struggling with mental and emotional health,

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:56.440
we pray to you. Lord, we know that you love us

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.440
and that you hear us, so we lift these names and situations

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:04.599
up to you.

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:34.440
For the names and the moments that we have spoken aloud and for those that we have kept

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:38.440
in our hearts, we pray to you that they may have life

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:42.440
and light, healing and hope,

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:46.440
peace, and a deep sense of your presence.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:50.440
Amen.

