00:38:28.439 --> 00:38:30.439
Verses 6-9 read,

00:38:30.439 --> 00:38:32.439
Pray for the peace of Jerusalem.

00:38:32.439 --> 00:38:34.439
May they prosper who love you.

00:38:34.439 --> 00:38:36.439
Peace be within your walls

00:38:36.439 --> 00:38:38.439
and security within your towers.

00:38:38.439 --> 00:38:40.439
For the sake of my relatives

00:38:40.439 --> 00:38:42.439
and friends, I will say,

00:38:42.439 --> 00:38:44.439
Peace be within you.

00:38:44.439 --> 00:38:46.439
For the sake of the house of the Lord our God,

00:38:46.439 --> 00:38:48.439
I will seek your good.

00:38:48.439 --> 00:38:50.439
What a beautiful prayer.

00:38:50.439 --> 00:38:52.439
And yet I read this and I couldn't help

00:38:52.439 --> 00:38:54.439
but to think of the way that peace

00:38:54.439 --> 00:38:56.439
is not in fact within

00:38:56.439 --> 00:38:58.439
Jerusalem's walls and towers

00:38:58.439 --> 00:39:00.439
today.

00:39:00.439 --> 00:39:02.439
Jerusalem has been in its latest

00:39:02.439 --> 00:39:04.439
conflict for more than a year

00:39:04.439 --> 00:39:06.439
now, beginning more than

00:39:06.439 --> 00:39:08.439
a year ago from an assault from Hamas

00:39:08.439 --> 00:39:10.439
in October of 2024.

00:39:10.439 --> 00:39:12.439
But what causes me more dissonance

00:39:12.439 --> 00:39:14.439
is to wonder

00:39:14.439 --> 00:39:16.439
how to pray for the peace of

00:39:16.439 --> 00:39:18.439
Jerusalem when Israel

00:39:18.439 --> 00:39:20.439
has itself become a perpetrator

00:39:20.439 --> 00:39:22.439
of great violence and death

00:39:22.439 --> 00:39:24.439
against so many Palestinians

00:39:24.439 --> 00:39:26.439
in Gaza.

00:39:26.439 --> 00:39:28.439
I want to pray for peace and for the good of Gaza

00:39:28.439 --> 00:39:30.439
who Israel would consider

00:39:30.439 --> 00:39:32.439
an enemy.

00:39:32.439 --> 00:39:34.439
More dissonance.

00:39:36.439 --> 00:39:38.439
I turn next to the New Testament text

00:39:38.439 --> 00:39:40.439
from Romans 13 in verses

00:39:40.439 --> 00:39:42.439
11 and 12. The Apostle

00:39:42.439 --> 00:39:44.439
Paul writes, Salvation

00:39:44.439 --> 00:39:46.439
is nearer to us

00:39:46.439 --> 00:39:48.439
than when we became believers

00:39:48.439 --> 00:39:50.439
first. The night is far

00:39:50.439 --> 00:39:52.439
gone. The day

00:39:52.439 --> 00:39:54.439
is near.

00:39:54.439 --> 00:39:56.439
Is it really, Paul?

00:39:56.439 --> 00:39:58.439
The night is far

00:39:58.439 --> 00:40:00.439
gone? Did that really

00:40:00.439 --> 00:40:02.439
come true? With all

00:40:02.439 --> 00:40:04.439
that's going on in the world some 2,000

00:40:04.439 --> 00:40:06.439
years later, with the violence

00:40:06.439 --> 00:40:08.439
against undocumented immigrants,

00:40:08.439 --> 00:40:10.439
with the scapegoating and

00:40:10.439 --> 00:40:12.439
unjust treatment of our transgender

00:40:12.439 --> 00:40:14.439
siblings, with all the

00:40:14.439 --> 00:40:16.439
war and atrocity that we've already

00:40:16.439 --> 00:40:18.439
mentioned, it feels like

00:40:18.439 --> 00:40:20.439
we are in the dead of night, bro.

00:40:22.439 --> 00:40:24.439
Surely

00:40:24.439 --> 00:40:26.439
Jesus has something helpful to say.

00:40:26.439 --> 00:40:28.439
The Gospel text is from Matthew

00:40:28.439 --> 00:40:30.439
24, where Jesus talks

00:40:30.439 --> 00:40:32.439
about what some interpret as

00:40:32.439 --> 00:40:34.439
the rapture. Two will be in

00:40:34.439 --> 00:40:36.439
the field, one will be taken, the other left.

00:40:36.439 --> 00:40:38.439
Two women will be grinding meal

00:40:38.439 --> 00:40:40.439
together, one will be taken, the other left.

00:40:40.439 --> 00:40:42.439
I am so glad that Brett

00:40:42.439 --> 00:40:44.439
solved all the problems of the rapture in the

00:40:44.439 --> 00:40:46.439
eschatology series this fall, so

00:40:46.439 --> 00:40:48.439
I can just move right past that

00:40:48.439 --> 00:40:50.439
to Jesus' punchline

00:40:50.439 --> 00:40:52.439
where he says,

00:40:52.439 --> 00:40:54.439
you don't know when the Lord is coming,

00:40:54.439 --> 00:40:56.439
so stay awake, be alert,

00:40:56.439 --> 00:40:58.439
be ready. The Son of Man is coming

00:40:58.439 --> 00:41:00.439
at an hour you don't

00:41:00.439 --> 00:41:02.439
expect. I don't

00:41:02.439 --> 00:41:04.439
know about you, but this text

00:41:04.439 --> 00:41:06.439
brings all my hell trauma right

00:41:06.439 --> 00:41:08.439
to the surface.

00:41:08.439 --> 00:41:10.439
Be ready or else Jesus will

00:41:10.439 --> 00:41:12.439
get you. Don't misbehave

00:41:12.439 --> 00:41:14.439
because Jesus might

00:41:14.439 --> 00:41:16.439
return right in the middle of it.

00:41:16.439 --> 00:41:18.439
I can hear that old Gospel preacher

00:41:18.439 --> 00:41:20.439
stoking fear

00:41:20.439 --> 00:41:22.439
to get folks to comply and obey

00:41:22.439 --> 00:41:24.439
with the church's moral norms.

00:41:24.439 --> 00:41:26.439
I mean, the Son of Man is even compared

00:41:26.439 --> 00:41:28.439
to a thief who comes in the middle

00:41:28.439 --> 00:41:30.439
of the night to rob someone.

00:41:30.439 --> 00:41:32.439
Stay awake so you don't get robbed.

00:41:32.439 --> 00:41:34.439
That's not a heartwarming

00:41:34.439 --> 00:41:36.439
image.

00:41:36.439 --> 00:41:38.439
More

00:41:38.439 --> 00:41:40.439
dissonance. Sorry

00:41:40.439 --> 00:41:42.439
to be such a downer, y'all.

00:41:44.439 --> 00:41:46.439
Maybe, just

00:41:46.439 --> 00:41:48.439
maybe you feel some of

00:41:48.439 --> 00:41:50.439
this dissonance yourself.

00:41:50.439 --> 00:41:52.439
The dissonance

00:41:52.439 --> 00:41:54.439
between the world we

00:41:54.439 --> 00:41:56.439
currently live in

00:41:56.439 --> 00:41:58.439
and the world that is promised

00:41:58.439 --> 00:42:00.439
to arrive one day.

00:42:00.439 --> 00:42:02.439
It seems

00:42:02.439 --> 00:42:04.439
better to be honest

00:42:04.439 --> 00:42:06.439
about the dissonance

00:42:06.439 --> 00:42:08.439
than to try to spiritually bypass

00:42:08.439 --> 00:42:10.439
it or to sugarcoat

00:42:10.439 --> 00:42:12.439
it or ignore

00:42:12.439 --> 00:42:14.439
it. This dissonance

00:42:14.439 --> 00:42:16.439
is exactly where I

00:42:16.439 --> 00:42:18.439
long for God to meet

00:42:18.439 --> 00:42:20.439
me, to meet us

00:42:20.439 --> 00:42:22.439
in this Advent

00:42:22.439 --> 00:42:24.439
season. What would it look

00:42:24.439 --> 00:42:26.439
like for God to meet

00:42:26.439 --> 00:42:28.439
us in the midst of this dissonance?

00:42:28.439 --> 00:42:30.439
To hold this dissonance

00:42:30.439 --> 00:42:32.439
with us? To lead

00:42:32.439 --> 00:42:34.439
us through it

00:42:34.439 --> 00:42:36.439
instead of around it?

00:42:36.439 --> 00:42:38.439
That's exactly what I

00:42:38.439 --> 00:42:40.439
wondered as I sat with these

00:42:40.439 --> 00:42:42.439
texts. God, what do we do with this?

00:42:42.439 --> 00:42:44.439
What's your

00:42:44.439 --> 00:42:46.439
invitation to us in the midst

00:42:46.439 --> 00:42:48.439
of dissonance like this?

00:42:48.439 --> 00:42:50.439
What does it look like for us to

00:42:50.439 --> 00:42:52.439
faithfully anticipate your

00:42:52.439 --> 00:42:54.439
arrival in this

00:42:54.439 --> 00:42:56.439
Advent season?

00:42:56.439 --> 00:42:58.439
I'll admit that I came to

00:42:58.439 --> 00:43:00.439
these texts with some ideas

00:43:00.439 --> 00:43:02.439
about what we might do with

00:43:02.439 --> 00:43:04.439
the dissonance instead of avoiding it

00:43:04.439 --> 00:43:06.439
to move through it, to let God sit

00:43:06.439 --> 00:43:08.439
with us in it,

00:43:08.439 --> 00:43:10.439
to lament the dissonance

00:43:10.439 --> 00:43:12.439
to God,

00:43:12.439 --> 00:43:14.439
to share our frustration and

00:43:14.439 --> 00:43:16.439
confusion and even anger with

00:43:16.439 --> 00:43:18.439
God. Lament, after all, is a

00:43:18.439 --> 00:43:20.439
very common response to dissonance

00:43:20.439 --> 00:43:22.439
in the Psalms.

00:43:22.439 --> 00:43:24.439
And certainly I commend lament

00:43:24.439 --> 00:43:26.439
as a healing practice.

00:43:26.439 --> 00:43:28.439
But as I read

00:43:28.439 --> 00:43:30.439
through the texts again

00:43:30.439 --> 00:43:32.439
and again, I began to notice something

00:43:32.439 --> 00:43:34.439
else that addressed this

00:43:34.439 --> 00:43:36.439
dissonance, that gave me

00:43:36.439 --> 00:43:38.439
something to hold on

00:43:38.439 --> 00:43:40.439
to. Jesus

00:43:40.439 --> 00:43:42.439
mentions it in Matthew 24 when he

00:43:42.439 --> 00:43:44.439
says, keep awake,

00:43:44.439 --> 00:43:46.439
be ready. Paul

00:43:46.439 --> 00:43:48.439
mentions it in Romans 13

00:43:48.439 --> 00:43:50.439
when he says, let us walk

00:43:50.439 --> 00:43:52.439
decently as in

00:43:52.439 --> 00:43:54.439
the day. Put on

00:43:54.439 --> 00:43:56.439
the Lord Jesus

00:43:56.439 --> 00:43:58.439
Christ. And what do you know?

00:43:58.439 --> 00:44:00.439
There it is at the end of

00:44:00.439 --> 00:44:02.439
our Isaiah text.

00:44:02.439 --> 00:44:04.439
O house of Jacob,

00:44:04.439 --> 00:44:06.439
come, let us

00:44:06.439 --> 00:44:08.439
walk in the light

00:44:08.439 --> 00:44:10.439
of the Lord.

00:44:10.439 --> 00:44:12.439
What I hear Jesus

00:44:12.439 --> 00:44:14.439
and Paul and Isaiah saying

00:44:14.439 --> 00:44:16.439
is that one way we can

00:44:16.439 --> 00:44:18.439
respond to this

00:44:18.439 --> 00:44:20.439
dissonance is with our

00:44:20.439 --> 00:44:22.439
lives. By

00:44:22.439 --> 00:44:24.439
embodying here and now

00:44:24.439 --> 00:44:26.439
in the midst of the dumpster

00:44:26.439 --> 00:44:28.439
fire of things,

00:44:28.439 --> 00:44:30.439
the future peace and

00:44:30.439 --> 00:44:32.439
goodness and justice

00:44:32.439 --> 00:44:34.439
for which we long.

00:44:34.439 --> 00:44:36.439
That's what Isaiah means

00:44:36.439 --> 00:44:38.439
when he invites Israel to walk

00:44:38.439 --> 00:44:40.439
in the light of the Lord, to walk

00:44:40.439 --> 00:44:42.439
in the ways of God,

00:44:42.439 --> 00:44:44.439
to embody in the present

00:44:44.439 --> 00:44:46.439
the peace and justice

00:44:46.439 --> 00:44:48.439
that is coming more fully

00:44:48.439 --> 00:44:50.439
in the future when all

00:44:50.439 --> 00:44:52.439
will stream to the mountain of God

00:44:52.439 --> 00:44:54.439
and be instructed in God's ways,

00:44:54.439 --> 00:44:56.439
when humanity will repurpose

00:44:56.439 --> 00:44:58.439
its war weapons into

00:44:58.439 --> 00:45:00.439
creation tools.

00:45:00.439 --> 00:45:02.439
What if walking in the light

00:45:02.439 --> 00:45:04.439
of the Lord means that

00:45:04.439 --> 00:45:06.439
we go ahead and start

00:45:06.439 --> 00:45:08.439
living the future

00:45:08.439 --> 00:45:10.439
now?

00:45:10.439 --> 00:45:12.439
What if the most faithful form

00:45:12.439 --> 00:45:14.439
of waiting is practicing

00:45:14.439 --> 00:45:16.439
the good way of Jesus

00:45:16.439 --> 00:45:18.439
right now?

00:45:18.439 --> 00:45:20.439
To put on the Lord

00:45:20.439 --> 00:45:22.439
Jesus Christ, as Paul says.

00:45:22.439 --> 00:45:24.439
The vibe of

00:45:24.439 --> 00:45:26.439
this invitation is not that it's all

00:45:26.439 --> 00:45:28.439
up to us, as if God's not

00:45:28.439 --> 00:45:30.439
going to do it and so we've got to create a different

00:45:30.439 --> 00:45:32.439
world on our own kind of thing.

00:45:32.439 --> 00:45:34.439
What if God is already

00:45:34.439 --> 00:45:36.439
doing it? What if God has

00:45:36.439 --> 00:45:38.439
always been doing it?

00:45:38.439 --> 00:45:40.439
What if God's

00:45:40.439 --> 00:45:42.439
at work to heal and

00:45:42.439 --> 00:45:44.439
renew and restore and our

00:45:44.439 --> 00:45:46.439
invitation is to

00:45:46.439 --> 00:45:48.439
participate in it?

00:45:48.439 --> 00:45:50.439
Isaiah's invitation

00:45:50.439 --> 00:45:52.439
after all is to walk by the light

00:45:52.439 --> 00:45:54.439
of the Lord.

00:45:54.439 --> 00:45:56.439
We don't have to generate the light.

00:45:56.439 --> 00:45:58.439
The light doesn't begin with

00:45:58.439 --> 00:46:00.439
us. We just have to find it

00:46:00.439 --> 00:46:02.439
and walk in it.

00:46:02.439 --> 00:46:04.439
Neither is the vibe

00:46:04.439 --> 00:46:06.439
of this invitation to

00:46:06.439 --> 00:46:08.439
walk in the light of the Lord or

00:46:08.439 --> 00:46:10.439
else.

00:46:10.439 --> 00:46:12.439
Thanks be to God. Contrary

00:46:12.439 --> 00:46:14.439
to my anxieties. Or

00:46:14.439 --> 00:46:16.439
else God will get us. Or else God

00:46:16.439 --> 00:46:18.439
will judge us and send us to hell.

00:46:18.439 --> 00:46:20.439
It's more like the plea of

00:46:20.439 --> 00:46:22.439
someone who loves us all

00:46:22.439 --> 00:46:24.439
so dearly. Please.

00:46:24.439 --> 00:46:26.439
Please walk

00:46:26.439 --> 00:46:28.439
in the light

00:46:28.439 --> 00:46:30.439
because the fruit of walking in the

00:46:30.439 --> 00:46:32.439
light is light.

00:46:32.439 --> 00:46:34.439
And the fruit of walking in darkness

00:46:34.439 --> 00:46:36.439
is darkness. What

00:46:36.439 --> 00:46:38.439
fruit do we want?

00:46:38.439 --> 00:46:40.439
God doesn't coerce

00:46:40.439 --> 00:46:42.439
or threaten us.

00:46:42.439 --> 00:46:44.439
The plea comes to us

00:46:44.439 --> 00:46:46.439
as an invitation to participate.

00:46:46.439 --> 00:46:48.439
To join in what the

00:46:48.439 --> 00:46:50.439
spirit of God is doing. To clothe

00:46:50.439 --> 00:46:52.439
ourselves with the character

00:46:52.439 --> 00:46:54.439
and action

00:46:54.439 --> 00:46:56.439
of Jesus.

00:46:56.439 --> 00:46:58.439
This invitation reminds me of something I've

00:46:58.439 --> 00:47:00.439
heard my co-director in the

00:47:00.439 --> 00:47:02.439
Healing Collective, Mallory

00:47:02.439 --> 00:47:04.439
Wyckoff say.

00:47:04.439 --> 00:47:06.439
That the best critique

00:47:06.439 --> 00:47:08.439
of the bad

00:47:08.439 --> 00:47:10.439
is the embodiment of the better.

00:47:10.439 --> 00:47:12.439
The best critique

00:47:12.439 --> 00:47:14.439
of the bad is the

00:47:14.439 --> 00:47:16.439
embodiment of the better.

00:47:16.439 --> 00:47:18.439
I love that. I feel like it's a place

00:47:18.439 --> 00:47:20.439
that I can put my dissonant

00:47:20.439 --> 00:47:22.439
energy. Instead of getting

00:47:22.439 --> 00:47:24.439
stuck in the dissonance,

00:47:24.439 --> 00:47:26.439
paralyzed by it. What if that was

00:47:26.439 --> 00:47:28.439
the energy that fueled me, that

00:47:28.439 --> 00:47:30.439
fueled us to embody

00:47:30.439 --> 00:47:32.439
the better. The best critique

00:47:32.439 --> 00:47:34.439
of war is

00:47:34.439 --> 00:47:36.439
the embodiment of peace.

00:47:36.439 --> 00:47:38.439
The best critique of scarcity

00:47:38.439 --> 00:47:40.439
is the embodiment of provision.

00:47:40.439 --> 00:47:42.439
The best critique of loneliness

00:47:42.439 --> 00:47:44.439
is the embodiment

00:47:44.439 --> 00:47:46.439
of belonging. The best

00:47:46.439 --> 00:47:48.439
critique of polarization

00:47:48.439 --> 00:47:50.439
is the embodiment of proximity.

00:47:50.439 --> 00:47:52.439
The best critique

00:47:52.439 --> 00:47:54.439
of apathy

00:47:54.439 --> 00:47:56.439
is the embodiment of

00:47:56.439 --> 00:47:58.439
empathy. The best

00:47:58.439 --> 00:48:00.439
critique of dehumanization

00:48:00.439 --> 00:48:02.439
is the embodiment of

00:48:02.439 --> 00:48:04.439
kindness. The

00:48:04.439 --> 00:48:06.439
best critique of injustice

00:48:06.439 --> 00:48:08.439
is the embodiment of

00:48:08.439 --> 00:48:10.439
love.

00:48:10.439 --> 00:48:12.439
A couple

00:48:12.439 --> 00:48:14.439
weeks ago I accepted an invitation

00:48:14.439 --> 00:48:16.439
from my friend and colleague

00:48:16.439 --> 00:48:18.439
Colin Packer to

00:48:18.439 --> 00:48:20.439
join him and another

00:48:20.439 --> 00:48:22.439
friend of ours, David Park,

00:48:22.439 --> 00:48:24.439
at the Dallas Field

00:48:24.439 --> 00:48:26.439
Office of Immigration

00:48:26.439 --> 00:48:28.439
and Customs Enforcement,

00:48:28.439 --> 00:48:30.439
also known as ICE.

00:48:30.439 --> 00:48:32.439
Colin had been

00:48:32.439 --> 00:48:34.439
invited by a grassroots

00:48:34.439 --> 00:48:36.439
organization called

00:48:36.439 --> 00:48:38.439
Vicinos Unidos, DFW,

00:48:38.439 --> 00:48:40.439
led by several Chicana

00:48:40.439 --> 00:48:42.439
women who are showing up

00:48:42.439 --> 00:48:44.439
every day at the field

00:48:44.439 --> 00:48:46.439
office to help migrant folks

00:48:46.439 --> 00:48:48.439
know their rights and to raise

00:48:48.439 --> 00:48:50.439
awareness about the mistreatment

00:48:50.439 --> 00:48:52.439
of our undocumented neighbors

00:48:52.439 --> 00:48:54.439
by ICE.

00:48:54.439 --> 00:48:56.439
Colin and David and I were there

00:48:56.439 --> 00:48:58.439
and we were invited specifically

00:48:58.439 --> 00:49:00.439
because we are white

00:49:00.439 --> 00:49:02.439
clergy persons.

00:49:02.439 --> 00:49:04.439
Unfortunately and not

00:49:04.439 --> 00:49:06.439
surprisingly, ICE agents

00:49:06.439 --> 00:49:08.439
respond much differently

00:49:08.439 --> 00:49:10.439
to white male clergy members

00:49:10.439 --> 00:49:12.439
than they do to our brown

00:49:12.439 --> 00:49:14.439
female colleagues.

00:49:14.439 --> 00:49:16.439
They yell and curse and make threats to brown

00:49:16.439 --> 00:49:18.439
women, but when a white clergy

00:49:18.439 --> 00:49:20.439
person is present, they

00:49:20.439 --> 00:49:22.439
are respectful and calm.

00:49:22.439 --> 00:49:24.439
So our invitation

00:49:24.439 --> 00:49:26.439
was to show up and share

00:49:26.439 --> 00:49:28.439
the privilege that comes with our being

00:49:28.439 --> 00:49:30.439
white to our non-white colleagues

00:49:30.439 --> 00:49:32.439
so that they could do their work

00:49:32.439 --> 00:49:34.439
more safely, more

00:49:34.439 --> 00:49:36.439
effectively.

00:49:36.439 --> 00:49:38.439
The leaders of Vicinos

00:49:38.439 --> 00:49:40.439
Unidos asked us to find some

00:49:40.439 --> 00:49:42.439
way to identify ourselves

00:49:42.439 --> 00:49:44.439
as clergy with either

00:49:44.439 --> 00:49:46.439
a stole or a collar, and that's why

00:49:46.439 --> 00:49:48.439
I'm wearing this tonight.

00:49:48.439 --> 00:49:50.439
Both so that ICE would

00:49:50.439 --> 00:49:52.439
know that we were clergy,

00:49:52.439 --> 00:49:54.439
but also so that our

00:49:54.439 --> 00:49:56.439
neighbors would not wonder if

00:49:56.439 --> 00:49:58.439
we were casual ICE agents

00:49:58.439 --> 00:50:00.439
ourselves and become

00:50:00.439 --> 00:50:02.439
suspicious of

00:50:02.439 --> 00:50:04.439
Vicinos Unidos

00:50:04.439 --> 00:50:06.439
and their work there.

00:50:06.439 --> 00:50:08.439
So we borrowed three stoles, one

00:50:08.439 --> 00:50:10.439
of which I'm wearing from our

00:50:10.439 --> 00:50:12.439
dear friend and colleague, Pepa Paniagua,

00:50:12.439 --> 00:50:14.439
who some of you know.

00:50:14.439 --> 00:50:16.439
She's a Presbyterian minister

00:50:16.439 --> 00:50:18.439
and she's got stoles and spades

00:50:18.439 --> 00:50:20.439
apparently.

00:50:20.439 --> 00:50:22.439
It's the first time I've ever worn one.

00:50:22.439 --> 00:50:24.439
This is the second time I've ever worn one.

00:50:24.439 --> 00:50:26.439
It feels a little weird, honestly,

00:50:26.439 --> 00:50:28.439
but isn't it pretty? It's so beautiful.

00:50:28.439 --> 00:50:30.439
Yeah?

00:50:30.439 --> 00:50:32.439
So one Friday,

00:50:32.439 --> 00:50:34.439
a couple weeks ago, we arrived

00:50:34.439 --> 00:50:36.439
a little bit before 6 a.m.

00:50:36.439 --> 00:50:38.439
in our stoles.

00:50:38.439 --> 00:50:40.439
We met the team, we stood on the sidewalk

00:50:40.439 --> 00:50:42.439
outside the field office, ready

00:50:42.439 --> 00:50:44.439
to help however we were needed, but

00:50:44.439 --> 00:50:46.439
mostly just to stand

00:50:46.439 --> 00:50:48.439
there.

00:50:48.439 --> 00:50:50.439
Occasionally cars would come toward us

00:50:50.439 --> 00:50:52.439
down this industrial

00:50:52.439 --> 00:50:54.439
West Dallas street, and if

00:50:54.439 --> 00:50:56.439
the cars were moving fast and sometimes

00:50:56.439 --> 00:50:58.439
blaring music, they were probably

00:50:58.439 --> 00:51:00.439
ICE agents checking in

00:51:00.439 --> 00:51:02.439
for their shift. I noticed

00:51:02.439 --> 00:51:04.439
in big letters on the back of

00:51:04.439 --> 00:51:06.439
one truck entering the employee

00:51:06.439 --> 00:51:08.439
parking lot, Jesus saves.

00:51:08.439 --> 00:51:10.439
I could feel

00:51:10.439 --> 00:51:12.439
the tension and anger in my

00:51:12.439 --> 00:51:14.439
body as those cars

00:51:14.439 --> 00:51:16.439
raced by, many without license

00:51:16.439 --> 00:51:18.439
plates, so that they couldn't

00:51:18.439 --> 00:51:20.439
be identified. I noticed

00:51:20.439 --> 00:51:22.439
as I looked over that my

00:51:22.439 --> 00:51:24.439
friend and colleague David was

00:51:24.439 --> 00:51:26.439
waving at the ICE agents

00:51:26.439 --> 00:51:28.439
as they came in.

00:51:28.439 --> 00:51:30.439
And that humanized them

00:51:30.439 --> 00:51:32.439
for me. I was like, oh, I needed that.

00:51:32.439 --> 00:51:34.439
I felt the difference,

00:51:34.439 --> 00:51:36.439
the opposition there.

00:51:36.439 --> 00:51:38.439
And some would see the

00:51:38.439 --> 00:51:40.439
stoles and they would wave back at us.

00:51:40.439 --> 00:51:42.439
Oh, something

00:51:42.439 --> 00:51:44.439
felt shifted.

00:51:46.439 --> 00:51:48.439
We wondered if

00:51:48.439 --> 00:51:50.439
they were worried about their own families.

00:51:50.439 --> 00:51:52.439
We wondered if their families

00:51:52.439 --> 00:51:54.439
were worried about them.

00:51:54.439 --> 00:51:56.439
If the cars were

00:51:56.439 --> 00:51:58.439
moving slowly down the street,

00:51:58.439 --> 00:52:00.439
they were usually our neighbors showing up

00:52:00.439 --> 00:52:02.439
for their immigration

00:52:02.439 --> 00:52:04.439
check-in appointments.

00:52:04.439 --> 00:52:06.439
Our colleagues would wave down the slow

00:52:06.439 --> 00:52:08.439
moving cars and invite them to talk.

00:52:08.439 --> 00:52:10.439
And if they were willing, they would pull in to

00:52:10.439 --> 00:52:12.439
an adjacent parking lot where

00:52:12.439 --> 00:52:14.439
our colleagues would let them know that ICE

00:52:14.439 --> 00:52:16.439
was detaining high numbers

00:52:16.439 --> 00:52:18.439
of people showing up

00:52:18.439 --> 00:52:20.439
for their routine

00:52:20.439 --> 00:52:22.439
immigration check-ins. They encouraged

00:52:22.439 --> 00:52:24.439
them to sign a form that would

00:52:24.439 --> 00:52:26.439
allow Vecinos Unidos

00:52:26.439 --> 00:52:28.439
to contact their family,

00:52:28.439 --> 00:52:30.439
to be able to track them in the

00:52:30.439 --> 00:52:32.439
system, otherwise there'd be no way

00:52:32.439 --> 00:52:34.439
to know where they went,

00:52:34.439 --> 00:52:36.439
where they were, what their

00:52:36.439 --> 00:52:38.439
status was.

00:52:38.439 --> 00:52:40.439
Detainees are sometimes transferred out

00:52:40.439 --> 00:52:42.439
of state on purpose to

00:52:42.439 --> 00:52:44.439
make it difficult to impede

00:52:44.439 --> 00:52:46.439
their deportation process.

00:52:46.439 --> 00:52:48.439
Our colleagues

00:52:48.439 --> 00:52:50.439
also encouraged them to park

00:52:50.439 --> 00:52:52.439
in the adjacent lot and not in

00:52:52.439 --> 00:52:54.439
the ICE parking lot because

00:52:54.439 --> 00:52:56.439
ICE has contracts with

00:52:56.439 --> 00:52:58.439
local towing companies to impound

00:52:58.439 --> 00:53:00.439
cars that stay in their

00:53:00.439 --> 00:53:02.439
lot. If they came with family

00:53:02.439 --> 00:53:04.439
members, our colleagues encouraged

00:53:04.439 --> 00:53:06.439
their family members to leave

00:53:06.439 --> 00:53:08.439
because ICE agents would

00:53:08.439 --> 00:53:10.439
often ask, do you have family waiting

00:53:10.439 --> 00:53:12.439
for you? And if they do, it's

00:53:12.439 --> 00:53:14.439
not uncommon for ICE to go out

00:53:14.439 --> 00:53:16.439
in the parking lot and detain

00:53:16.439 --> 00:53:18.439
the family members as well.

00:53:18.439 --> 00:53:20.439
Occasionally

00:53:20.439 --> 00:53:22.439
we were asked to pray for

00:53:22.439 --> 00:53:24.439
our neighbors who were walking to

00:53:24.439 --> 00:53:26.439
the field office for their appointments.

00:53:26.439 --> 00:53:28.439
And we prayed for peace

00:53:28.439 --> 00:53:30.439
and protection

00:53:30.439 --> 00:53:32.439
as they trembled.

00:53:32.439 --> 00:53:34.439
Sometimes clergy

00:53:34.439 --> 00:53:36.439
members were asked to

00:53:36.439 --> 00:53:38.439
escort our colleagues and

00:53:38.439 --> 00:53:40.439
neighbors to the door of the field

00:53:40.439 --> 00:53:42.439
office to inquire about their family members

00:53:42.439 --> 00:53:44.439
who had been inside for longer than

00:53:44.439 --> 00:53:46.439
expected and might be

00:53:46.439 --> 00:53:48.439
detained. I watched as one pregnant woman

00:53:48.439 --> 00:53:50.439
came back with her

00:53:50.439 --> 00:53:52.439
small child

00:53:52.439 --> 00:53:54.439
and returned from asking about her husband.

00:53:54.439 --> 00:53:56.439
She wept

00:53:56.439 --> 00:53:58.439
as she learned that he had been detained.

00:53:58.439 --> 00:54:00.439
Our colleagues gave her a place to

00:54:00.439 --> 00:54:02.439
sit and food to eat.

00:54:02.439 --> 00:54:04.439
They played with her son as

00:54:04.439 --> 00:54:06.439
she processed the news that

00:54:06.439 --> 00:54:08.439
she had just received.

00:54:08.439 --> 00:54:10.439
I listened as David asked

00:54:10.439 --> 00:54:12.439
Noemi, one of the founders

00:54:12.439 --> 00:54:14.439
of Vicinos Unidos

00:54:14.439 --> 00:54:16.439
DFW, how she came

00:54:16.439 --> 00:54:18.439
into this work. And with

00:54:18.439 --> 00:54:20.439
tears in her eyes, she shared

00:54:20.439 --> 00:54:22.439
how her own father had

00:54:22.439 --> 00:54:24.439
been deported when she was young.

00:54:24.439 --> 00:54:26.439
She knows what

00:54:26.439 --> 00:54:28.439
it's like, and she wants to help

00:54:28.439 --> 00:54:30.439
other people who are in similar

00:54:30.439 --> 00:54:32.439
circumstances. And so

00:54:32.439 --> 00:54:34.439
she gets up every day

00:54:34.439 --> 00:54:36.439
early to come to the field office

00:54:36.439 --> 00:54:38.439
to help her neighbors

00:54:38.439 --> 00:54:40.439
before she goes in to

00:54:40.439 --> 00:54:42.439
her full-time job.

00:54:42.439 --> 00:54:44.439
Noemi might not

00:54:44.439 --> 00:54:46.439
use this language, but she and

00:54:46.439 --> 00:54:48.439
her colleagues are

00:54:48.439 --> 00:54:50.439
walking in the light of

00:54:50.439 --> 00:54:52.439
the Lord. In the

00:54:52.439 --> 00:54:54.439
midst of the dissonance of

00:54:54.439 --> 00:54:56.439
detention and mass

00:54:56.439 --> 00:54:58.439
deportation and mistreatment of

00:54:58.439 --> 00:55:00.439
undocumented neighbors, in the midst

00:55:00.439 --> 00:55:02.439
of injustice, they accepted

00:55:02.439 --> 00:55:04.439
the invitation to participate

00:55:04.439 --> 00:55:06.439
in God's peace

00:55:06.439 --> 00:55:08.439
and justice and

00:55:08.439 --> 00:55:10.439
goodness. To critique the bad

00:55:10.439 --> 00:55:12.439
by embodying

00:55:12.439 --> 00:55:14.439
the better. To anticipate

00:55:14.439 --> 00:55:16.439
with their active bodies

00:55:16.439 --> 00:55:18.439
the renewed and healed world

00:55:18.439 --> 00:55:20.439
that is to come. The world

00:55:20.439 --> 00:55:22.439
we hope for in the second

00:55:22.439 --> 00:55:24.439
coming of the Christ

00:55:24.439 --> 00:55:26.439
in this Advent season.

00:55:26.439 --> 00:55:28.439
I wonder,

00:55:28.439 --> 00:55:30.439
how might the

00:55:30.439 --> 00:55:32.439
Spirit be inviting you

00:55:32.439 --> 00:55:34.439
to walk in the light of the

00:55:34.439 --> 00:55:36.439
Lord this Advent?

00:55:36.439 --> 00:55:38.439
To embody the goodness

00:55:38.439 --> 00:55:40.439
of God.

00:55:40.439 --> 00:55:42.439
Where do you long

00:55:42.439 --> 00:55:44.439
for more peace

00:55:44.439 --> 00:55:46.439
and goodness and justice

00:55:46.439 --> 00:55:48.439
and belonging around you?

00:55:48.439 --> 00:55:50.439
What opportunities

00:55:50.439 --> 00:55:52.439
to embody

00:55:52.439 --> 00:55:54.439
those longings is the

00:55:54.439 --> 00:55:56.439
Spirit sending

00:55:56.439 --> 00:55:58.439
your way?

00:55:58.439 --> 00:56:00.439
We don't have to fabricate

00:56:00.439 --> 00:56:02.439
the opportunities.

00:56:02.439 --> 00:56:04.439
We simply have to pay attention

00:56:04.439 --> 00:56:06.439
for what the Spirit might be

00:56:06.439 --> 00:56:08.439
sending toward us

00:56:08.439 --> 00:56:10.439
and cooperate with it.

00:56:10.439 --> 00:56:12.439
Go with the flow

00:56:12.439 --> 00:56:14.439
of it. And if it

00:56:14.439 --> 00:56:16.439
seems daunting,

00:56:16.439 --> 00:56:18.439
I hear you. There's some risk

00:56:18.439 --> 00:56:20.439
in accepting such an invitation.

00:56:20.439 --> 00:56:22.439
I am usually pretty

00:56:22.439 --> 00:56:24.439
anxious to accept the invitation

00:56:24.439 --> 00:56:26.439
myself. So,

00:56:26.439 --> 00:56:28.439
it's normal. You're in good

00:56:28.439 --> 00:56:30.439
company. And I hope

00:56:30.439 --> 00:56:32.439
you'll be kind to yourself in the midst

00:56:32.439 --> 00:56:34.439
of the dauntingness of it.

00:56:34.439 --> 00:56:36.439
The good news is that

00:56:36.439 --> 00:56:38.439
the invitation is to

00:56:38.439 --> 00:56:40.439
us collectively.

00:56:40.439 --> 00:56:42.439
Let us walk

00:56:42.439 --> 00:56:44.439
in the light of the Lord.

00:56:44.439 --> 00:56:46.439
This embodiment work is something

00:56:46.439 --> 00:56:48.439
we get to do together.

00:56:48.439 --> 00:56:50.439
Something

00:56:50.439 --> 00:56:52.439
I got to do with my brothers, Colin

00:56:52.439 --> 00:56:54.439
and David.

00:56:54.439 --> 00:56:56.439
If we long for peace in our world,

00:56:56.439 --> 00:56:58.439
let us be a community

00:56:58.439 --> 00:57:00.439
of peace. If we

00:57:00.439 --> 00:57:02.439
long for belonging in our world,

00:57:02.439 --> 00:57:04.439
let us be a community

00:57:04.439 --> 00:57:06.439
of belonging.

00:57:06.439 --> 00:57:08.439
If we long for the recognition

00:57:08.439 --> 00:57:10.439
of the image of God in all of

00:57:10.439 --> 00:57:12.439
humanity, let us be a community

00:57:12.439 --> 00:57:14.439
that recognizes the image of God

00:57:14.439 --> 00:57:16.439
in each other.

00:57:16.439 --> 00:57:18.439
If we long for

00:57:18.439 --> 00:57:20.439
generosity in our world, let us be a

00:57:20.439 --> 00:57:22.439
community of generosity.

00:57:22.439 --> 00:57:24.439
If we long for justice in our

00:57:24.439 --> 00:57:26.439
world, let us be a community

00:57:26.439 --> 00:57:28.439
of justice.

00:57:28.439 --> 00:57:30.439
Come, let us

00:57:30.439 --> 00:57:32.439
walk in the light

00:57:32.439 --> 00:57:34.439
of the Lord.

00:57:34.439 --> 00:57:36.439
In the name of the Father, and of the

00:57:36.439 --> 00:57:38.439
Son, and the Holy Spirit.

00:57:38.439 --> 00:57:40.439
Amen.

00:57:44.439 --> 00:57:46.439
It is time for communion.

00:57:48.439 --> 00:57:50.439
At the table, we

00:57:50.439 --> 00:57:52.439
practice open communion.

00:57:52.439 --> 00:57:54.439
So, all are welcome to

00:57:54.439 --> 00:57:56.439
participate who wish to.

00:57:56.439 --> 00:57:58.439
We go row by row

00:57:58.439 --> 00:58:00.439
from the front to the back

00:58:00.439 --> 00:58:02.439
to this center aisle all the way up

00:58:02.439 --> 00:58:04.439
to receive the bread and the cup.

00:58:04.439 --> 00:58:06.439
As you take the cup,

00:58:06.439 --> 00:58:08.439
just know that the red is

00:58:08.439 --> 00:58:10.439
wine, and the white is juice.

00:58:10.439 --> 00:58:12.439
And you are welcome to

00:58:12.439 --> 00:58:14.439
spend some time in prayer, or kneeling

00:58:14.439 --> 00:58:16.439
up here at the front, or to return to your seat.

00:58:16.439 --> 00:58:18.439
Whatever is most comfortable

00:58:18.439 --> 00:58:20.439
and preferable to you.

00:58:20.439 --> 00:58:22.439
This is the

00:58:22.439 --> 00:58:24.439
table, not of

00:58:24.439 --> 00:58:26.439
the church, but of the Lord.

00:58:26.439 --> 00:58:28.439
It's made ready

00:58:28.439 --> 00:58:30.439
for those who love Him,

00:58:30.439 --> 00:58:32.439
and for those who want to love Him

00:58:32.439 --> 00:58:34.439
more. So, come.

00:58:34.439 --> 00:58:36.439
You who have much

00:58:36.439 --> 00:58:38.439
faith, and you who have

00:58:38.439 --> 00:58:40.439
little. You who have

00:58:40.439 --> 00:58:42.439
been here often, and you

00:58:42.439 --> 00:58:44.439
who have not been here long.

00:58:44.439 --> 00:58:46.439
You who have tried to follow,

00:58:46.439 --> 00:58:48.439
and you who have failed.

00:58:48.439 --> 00:58:50.439
Come, because

00:58:50.439 --> 00:58:52.439
it is the Lord who invites you.

00:58:52.439 --> 00:58:54.439
It's His will that those

00:58:54.439 --> 00:58:56.439
who want Him should meet

00:58:56.439 --> 00:58:58.439
Him here.

00:58:58.439 --> 00:59:00.439
Come to the table.

